{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114350-project-twilight-and-twin-peaks","id":1114350,"title":"Project: Twilight and Twin Peaks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-10T18:42:22-07:00","id":1114350,"title":"Project: Twilight and Twin Peaks","content":"The Project: Twilight book was technically a supplement for Werewolf: The Apocalypse despite the fact it was very much something that touched on all branches of the World of Darkness. However, what I loved most about that book was the sample adventure, which I never in my wildest dreams believed I would say about any supplement ever.<br /> <br /> It was <i>Twin Peaks: The Adventure</i> with plenty of inspiration from the source material but also enough differences not to be a rip off. You had the Nappy Napper (Ronin Metis child-killer) serving as the erstwhile BOB, a biker gang of Get who look like the bad guys but aren't, a Enticer serving as the Laura Palmer (though not quite dead yet), and a Pentex perfume executive being the Ben Horne of the place.<br /> <br /> Anyone else remember this adventure?<br /> <br /> Well, I'm thinking about expanding the town mentioned there and working on making a Werewolf: The Apocalypse game present where the PCs are Garou who have the unfortune job of reclaiming a caern in the area which is under high profile by the government's SAD and also Pentex without making waves for either.<br /> <br /> I was curious what sort of government-related problems I could throw at the PCs and what sort of advice you guys had for &quot;small town action roleplaying&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T19:12:31-07:00","id":1114359,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a lot of fun! If the caern is in Federal or State-protected land, that could prove a double-edged sword for a prospective sept. Also, the sheer number or supernaturals and strange events in the area is likely to have a cascading effect as others begin to wonder what's so important about the area. This could, in turn, draw all sorts of unwanted attention from not only the government, but also hunters, reporters, and even just nosy locals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T20:53:16-07:00","id":1114394,"title":"","content":"Twin Peaks in general is a huge inspiration for Werewolf to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T00:12:31-07:00","id":1114465,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine ran a chronicle in a creepy Idaho small town that was basically Twin Peaks dropped into the World of Darkness. He posted it over an Obsidian Portal <a href=\"http://witikofalls.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">page</a> you might take some inspiration from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T15:12:03-07:00","id":1114772,"title":"","content":"Small towns mean that the ordinary humans become much more important to the setting. Make sure you have plenty of ordinary NPCs for players to get to learn and interact with. Make them important to the setting. Twin Peaks wasn't just about Copper and the Black Lodge and all the weirdness. It was Deputy Andy, Lucy Moran, Audrey Horne, Ed Hurley, Norma Jennings, and Doc Hayward. Some of my favorite bits were the relationship between the Horne brothers (Ben and Jerry), the love triangle between Andy, Lucy, &amp; Dick Tremayne, and any scene where Pete Martell was in. The town itself isn't as important as the ordinary people in it. Most of these characters can probably be divided into greater families, and it may be best to design families and internal family dynamics first rather than individual characters. And you won't need to gen their stats. By making the individual people more prominent, you can expand the scope of the setting in the player's minds. They'll actually know their neighbors instead of being unknown NPC in the apartment next door to them.<br /> <br /> Second, show how these ordinary people are being impacted by whatever supernatural evil is out there. Not directly, but in unseen ways as the Banes triumph or are defeated in the umbra.<br /> <br /> Try to keep the ordinary people as ordinary as possible. Don't make them hedge wizards or psychic numina or even kinfolk (although I assume there will be some kinfolk families in town). At most, have a few people who can sense the Periphery (in the show, this is was mainly Major Griggs and the Log Lady, although the Log Lady might have a Merit as well). They can sense that something is going on, but aren't very sure what it is.<br /> <br /> Create your set piece encounters and map them out. Only some of them will be in the actual town itself. A lot will be out there in the surrounding undeveloped land which could be places for Umbral Domains or other secret plot stuff. Lots of things can happen outside of town where witnesses don't exist.<br /> <br /> Make sure you have some unique locations or mysteries for the characters to unravel. One Eyed Jack's, the Packard Mill, the Double R Dinner, the Great Northern Hotel, and the Red Room (an umbral domain) are practically characters in themselves. And outside the actual Palmer Murder investigation, you have other mysteries/threats like Horne's resort development, various love triangles, the drug trade, and the US Air Force presence. These can be linked to the main Black Lodge plot, but aren't obviously so.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T20:55:54-07:00","id":1114893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1114350-project-twilight-and-twin-peaks#post1114350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was curious what sort of government-related problems I could throw at the PCs...</div> </div> </div> </div>The old abandoned Harold &amp; Harold mine that the crazy ex-Bone Gnawer dude was using as a base gets reported by the FBI guys to the EPA and six months later gets listed as a Superfund site despite being practically right on top of (or, well, <i>underneath</i>) the caern. How would the <i>Get</i> deal with that? Like, it's great that it's going to (finally) get cleaned up, but hundreds of EPA contractors traipsing around the caern for years is decidedly <i>not</i>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T21:56:03-07:00","id":1114918,"title":"","content":"Ooh. That's a good one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T13:58:09-07:00","id":1117923,"title":"","content":"Hell, elements like Catherine Martell returning to town disguised as Mr. Tojamura and an amnesiac Nadine Hurley chasing after a high school boy while her husband watched helplessly are ripe fodder for drama without involving any supernatural presences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T01:40:55-07:00","id":1119208,"title":"","content":"Hey folks,<br /> <br /> I finally finished my UNDER A BLOOD RED MOON campaign which ended with the PCs getting feted but not QUITE as much as they should have been. They will find themselves &quot;given&quot; a &quot;great reward&quot; in the form of an old sept whose entire population was supposedly wiped out in the area. This is going to be the basis for the Project: Twilight adventure done from the Garou perspective.<br /> <br /> The PCs are going to go down to the town (which I need to come up with a snappy name for) and find it's a sleepy community with the sept having completely fallen apart and having not been cared for in a very long time. It's &quot;just&quot; a level 1 Caern, though having one all to yourself is never a bad thing either. It's also linked to a much larger and more powerful Caern in the woods but which will be a source of investigation.<br /> <br /> They will uncover there's been a series of murders in the area that will, of course, lead to the Nappy Napper and encounters with the Special Affairs Division. They will also discover the local Pentex plant is manufacturing Enticers. The nature of the adventure will involve some moral conundrums which I think should be enjoyable.<br /> <br /> * Do they spare the Laura Palmer-esque character or kill her so she doesn't become an Enticer? If they do spare her, will the Nappy Napper get her? Can they purifer her before she becomes a Formori or will they fail?<br /> <br /> * Will they kill or harm or work with the SAD officers? I'm inclined to think they will probably figure out the PCs are werewolves with one reacting berserk to them while the others being more open minded. I may also include a NWO agent among them, ironically one of the more open minded agents and the Agent Cooper analogue.<br /> <br /> (Why is the NWO agent more open-minded? Killing werewolves does nothing but befriending some could mean many many Garou secrets falling into the hands of the Technocracy--a betrayal for later in the campaign)<br /> <br /> * What do they do about the Pentex plant in their literal backyard? Killing the executives might get rid of the worst of the taint now but it'll also draw attention and they can just send new owners eventually.<br /> <br /> Once the opening adventure is done, I'm basically going to treat the Town as Twin Peaks. Everyone will be renamed with some elements shuffled around but that should be a source of interesting ideas and thoughts. The town will also have a number of other supernaturals inside it, including some Fera, but all of them are hiding from each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}